{# Lives inside the table's scroll box, under a hairline of its own: the row is
   part of the table, not a control that floats beneath it. It is also the
   table's bottom edge — without it the last row simply falls off — so the
   count is rendered whenever there are rows, whether or not there is a page
   either side of this one.

   Stuck to the bottom of that box (`do-pager-sticky`, client/dev-ops.css) and
   opaque against the rows travelling under it: Previous, Next and the count
   are no use to an operator who has to scroll twenty rows to reach them.

   The footer says how much of the stream is on screen, and only that: the
   count on the left, the two directions on the right. How fresh the data is
   belongs to the rollup strip at the top of the card, beside the counts it
   qualifies.

   The count says one fact: how many rows are on screen. It said the groups
   too, and a footer that reports both is a second summary of a page whose
   rollup strip already owns the folding — two arithmetics, in two places, for
   a reader who asked for neither.

   Both directions are always drawn. A page that renders only the link it has
   moves Next across the footer the moment Previous appears, so the button an
   operator is aiming at is somewhere else on the next page; the direction
   there is no page in is a muted span of the same size, in the same place.

   One cluster, hard right, rather than two links spaced by whatever the row
   happened to hold between them: `← Previous` and `Next →` are one control
   with two directions. `ml-auto` goes on the cluster, once, so both travel
   together at the right and nothing floats in the middle of the footer. #}
{# Medium, not the button's own weight: Previous and Next are the quietest
   controls on the card, and the two of them set in semibold outweighed the
   figures the footer exists to report. The muted span wears the same weight,
   so the unavailable direction is the same object, greyed. #}
{% set pagerLink = "btn btn-xs btn-ghost font-medium" %}
{% set pagerDisabled = "btn btn-xs btn-ghost font-medium text-base-content/30" %}
{% if params.count or params.previousHref or params.nextHref %}
  <nav class="do-pager-sticky flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-3.5 py-2" aria-label="Pagination" data-testid="do-pager">
    {% if params.count %}
      <span class="text-[11px] text-base-content/55" data-testid="do-pager-count">{{ params.count }} event{{ "" if params.count == 1 else "s" }}</span>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-2" data-testid="do-pager-links">
      {% if params.previousHref %}
        <a class="{{ pagerLink }}" rel="prev" href="{{ params.previousHref }}" data-testid="do-pager-previous">← Previous</a>
      {% else %}
        <span class="{{ pagerDisabled }}" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="do-pager-previous-disabled">← Previous</span>
      {% endif %}
      {% if params.nextHref %}
        <a class="{{ pagerLink }}" rel="next" href="{{ params.nextHref }}" data-testid="do-pager-next">Next →</a>
      {% else %}
        <span class="{{ pagerDisabled }}" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="do-pager-next-disabled">Next →</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </nav>
{% endif %}
